what's going on guys this is rob welcome  back to geek culture explained and we  are talking about the re-release of  spider-man no way home the more fun  stuff or as we like to call it the  awkward and uncut version so for those  of you guys who don't know the  spider-man no way home film was recently  re-released to theaters with 11 minutes  of extra footage that we simply just  didn't see in the theatrical cut because  it was removed for any number of reasons  such is the case when it comes to  hollywood films now one of the cool  things that happens here is that you see  andrew and toby and tom all of whom are  on a zoom call basically thanking  everybody for supporting them now this  is not officially part of the movie it's  them as actors thanking all of us as  fans who supported the three of them  coming together for the film and  honestly which one of us would not have  done that who's the one person because i  know one of you were who's the one  person that didn't want to see these  three guys in a movie together but for  toby tom and andrew you're welcome  and so i guess let's really cut to the  big question that a lot of people have  right what was the big post-credits  scene because we knew before this film  came out even though there were rumors  and we didn't know for certain that  there was basically a post-credits scene  that was in the film that was not in the  original theatrical release well the  cool thing about this is this actually  shows us how far reaching the effects  are of the spell that was cast to remove  everyone's knowledge of tom holland's  peter parker from existence and so what  happens in this post-credits scene is  betty brant who plays the school  reporter in midtown high is basically  showing a montage of various scenes and  clips and images and things like that  from essentially all the previous movies  that we'd seen and tom holland's peter  parker is nowhere to be seen in any of  those and so all the indications from  this post-credits scene seem to point to  the idea that every trace of peter's  existence every image every video the  whole nine yards he simply just isn't  there so it's not as though the way we  originally suspected in the post-credits  scene when the movie first came out that  simply his memory of his existence was  removed from everyone's minds every  trace of his existence was removed and  honestly i feel like some variation of  this should have been put in the  original film otherwise we wouldn't have  been asking this question in the first  place but this really seems to solidify  that that it's not simply that people  forgot peter parker it's as though he  never existed but the next deleted scene  we get into is a scene that features  harry holland the brother of tom holland  which was originally cut from the film  and actually disappointed both tom and  harry because of something that they  really really wanted to see but this  scene basically features harry holland  snatching a purse and then running  spider-man of course catches up to him  he strings him up on his webs and then  it's basically some banter i mean it's  people saying everything from reasonable  statements to just ridiculous statements  for example somebody says something  along the lines that teen brains are not  as developed as adult brains therefore  he's not equipped to be able to decide  who is a criminal and who is not and  even one person says something is  ridiculous is the fact that peter and  criminals are actually working in  cahoots and peter of course gives a  sarcastic reaction and saying no yeah  i'm working with him like that kind of a  thing which in all honesty that's a  funny little reference to the comics  because in the early days of  spider-man's adventures one of the  things that jay jonah jameson had put  forward is the idea that peter parker  and criminals were working together the  peter was actually making it possible or  giving criminals ideas for crimes that  peter would in turn swoop in and  basically stop them from committing in  order to guarantee his own reason and  success in the superhero landscape it's  ridiculous but it's still kind of cool  now the next deleted scene that we get  is the one where peter basically has his  interrogation scene with damage control  and this one's not overly important it  basically just gives more of the  interrogation from peter's perspective  so he talks about climbing the various  monuments we'd seen him climb in the  previous film and in fact they even  interrogate him a little bit more about  the whole night monkey persona that he  had for a little while but it just kind  of is a nice way to bring in some of his  previous actions from the other films is  it overly important no but it's still  kind of cool now the next deleted scene  that we get is one that focuses on happy  hogan damage control and matt murdock  also known as daredevil who we're all  very very excited to see in future mcu  projects and this one actually sort of  pigtails off of an existing scene that  we saw in the promos which was all the  villains just kind of awkwardly riding  up the escalator or the elevator rather  to happy hogan's apartment but when they  get there happy hogan is basically  dealing with damage control alongside  his attorney matt murdock now this scene  unfolds pretty much the way you would  expect it to with him being asked  various questions and interrogation  style and so on and so forth but there  is a moment very similar to the first  scene that we got in the movie with matt  murdock when he caught the brick if you  guys recall and i don't know why you  wouldn't somebody threw a brick through  the window and then matt murdock caught  it and spiderman was like how in the  hell did you catch that it's similar to  that in the sense that matt murdock  tells happy hogan to stop sweating even  though happy hogan is not visibly  sweating and so it's basically matt  murdock's senses picking up on the fact  that happy hogan is sweating even though  it can't really be discerned by the  naked eye now this is kind of a cool  little way to sort of segue into the  powers of matt murdock the fact that  he's able to use his enhanced senses to  detect things that people normally  wouldn't be able to pick up on it's not  the most important scene there ever was  but as far as daredevil goes it does add  a bit of expansion to what we already  know or have already seen about his  powers at least from daredevil and the  first spider-man no way home release and  what it is that he's capable of which i  love these small little touches i like  seeing these small little things  regarding matt murdock and what it is  that he's able to do given the various  powers that he has but there's another  deleted scene which is kind of like  peter's day at school kind of to a  degree but what it basically shows is  that people  while his identity is ousted to the  world and people know who he is they  kind of blend the line between treating  him like he's some kind of a freak and  then wanting him to do spider-man stuff  so they have them like crawl up walls  and things like that and then just keep  referring to him as a freak which is  kind of weird so they sort of split the  difference i don't know how overly  important this scene was and i'm not too  upset that it was removed from the movie  it was interesting but it wasn't really  necessary here's the reason why it  probably got cut in the first place but  probably one of the better scenes that  in all honesty i feel like should have  been included in the original theatrical  release but i can understand why it was  cut just simply due to timing is the  extended scene of the three spiderman  hanging out which was really really  amazing so you guys remember that scene  when the three of them were hanging out  and you get a smidgen of a conversation  about the bio webbing of toby it's  basically that right it's a little bit  of an extension of that and in fact they  kind of talk about the different things  they've done right the instance where  tom holland went into space in order to  stop thanos the instance where toby  mcguire is talking about having defeated  an alien symbiote obviously referring to  venom and then of course andrew garfield  didn't really do anything cool in his  spider-man movies except like when stacy  die and i don't even know if that's a  cool thing but that was really kind of  his moment to essentially sulk in the  scene and that's when he gets a bit of a  pick-me-up from toby mcguire who tells  him dude you're amazing right you can't  keep dumping on yourself or you have to  look at the things you've done and  simply just tell yourself you just  haven't reached the moment where you  fought a symbiote or something along  those lines so it's a cool instance to  see these characters relating in that  way and then of course as we know from  the various leaks and rumors that have  come out the statements made that we  should all do this again sometime and  then it's definitely so what this seems  to indicate is that for these three guys  andrew toby tom that it doesn't look  like we're simply going to see them  walking away and never reuniting again  which makes perfect sense and in fact we  have a video about that which will show  up here or here one of those places but  basically it'll be a video talking about  these three different spider-man and how  they could return with regards to the  larger spider-verse series of movies  that sony's making into the spider-verse  beyond spider-verse and how they're  seemingly building up to a giant  spider-verse-centric event that could  see these three spider-man and others  that we haven't seen yet or have seen  all reuniting to face off against some  common foe wouldn't it be awesome if the  entire spider-verse reunited to face off  and help the avengers and whoever else  defeat king the conqueror that would be  a massive event let me know what you  guys think down in the comments section  though have you guys seen the re-release  or have you guys not seen the re-release  and if you haven't seen it let me know  why i'm kind of curious but thank you  all for watching and we will catch you  all later  peace

